			"date": "2024-04-22T18:29:45.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Would you mind sharing any examples? No problem if you don't want to support Vercel/Next free of charge, or don't have time, but I use Next at work and would be open to making a PR with improvements for my team/product's sake (and my own satisfaction with our performance)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112316653839559656",
			"parentId": "112316290552173149",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/112316653839559656",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-04-22T20:02:09.143Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://hachyderm.io/@philw_\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>philw_</span></a></span> just working on some Eleventy Image comparisons, will probably highlight some of these at 11ty Conf. The biggest ones are: 1. the DX of requiring a static import for the image or you’ll need to specify a width/height. 2. The valid image widths are hardcoded as global configuration and not specific to the width you specify for the image (if I want my image to render 129px, it returns a 256px image on 1.0 DPR screen) 3. The classic complaint about unnecessary content-negotiation.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
